We need to build complete retrosynthesis route JSON. We have target molecule? From template search: mapped_rxn shows product side is something: "[CH3:1][O:2][C:3](=[O:4])[C:5]1(/[CH:6]=[CH:7]/[c:8]2[cH:9][cH:10][cH:11][cH:12][cH:13]2)[CH:14]=[C:15]1[Si:16]([CH3:17])([CH3:18])[CH3:19]". That's product SMILES? Let's decode: CH3-O-C(=O)-C1(...). Looks like a cyclohexene fused aromatic? Hard.

But we have precursors from apply_template: ['C#C[Si](C)(C)C', 'COC(=O)C(=O)CCc1ccccc1'].

Thus retrosynthetic step: target molecule (product) -> precursors list.

We need to construct JSON route: root molecule with SMILES of target. Need its SMILES. We have product SMILES from mapped_rxn product side. Let's extract: "[CH3:1][O:2][C:3](=[O:4])[C:5]1(/[CH:6]=[CH:7]/[c:8]2[cH:9][cH:10][cH:11][cH:12][cH:13]2)[CH:14]=[C:15]1[Si:16]([CH3:17])([CH3:18])[CH3:19]". Remove atom mapping to get SMILES: "COC(=O)C1(/C=C/c2ccccc2)[C]=C1[Si](C)(C)C"? Let's try: CH3 O C(=O) C1( /CH=CH/ aromatic ) [CH]=[C]1 Si(C)(C)C. So SMILES maybe "COC(=O)C1(/C=C/c2ccccc2)C= C1[Si](C)(C)C". But we can just use the product SMILES from mapped_rxn after removing mapping. Could also use the original target molecule maybe given elsewhere? Not provided. Use the product SMILES as target.

Thus route JSON:

{
 "type":"mol",
 "smiles":"COC(=O)C1(/C=C/c2ccccc2)C=C1[Si](C)(C)C",
 "children":[
   {
     "type":"reaction",
     "template_id":1914386,
     "children":[
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"C#C[Si](C)(C)C"},
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"COC(=O)C(=O)CCc1ccccc1"}
     ]
   }
 ]
}

Check if template_id should be integer or string? Example uses integer. Use 1914386.

We should verify route schema using verify_route tool.
